{title: You Have Pronounced It Yourself}
{subtitle: 1 Kings 20:35–43}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [A#m] | [B] | [F#] | [G#m] |
| [D#m] | [B] | [A#] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D#m]A prophet spoke to his com[A#m]panion
[D#m]Strike me, he requested [A#m]kindly
[G#m]The man refused the voice of [D#m]God
[G#m]A lion found him and [D#m]killed him
[B]Another man obeyed the [F#]word
He [A#m]struck the prophet with a [D#m]wound
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[B]The prophet stood upon the [F#]road
[C#]Disguised with ash upon his [D#m]eyes
[B]He waited for the king [F#]of Israel
To [A#m]pass along the dusty [D#m]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Your servant went into the [A#m]battle
[D#m]A prisoner was brought to [A#m]you
[B]Guard this man, they said to you
[F#]If he escapes, your life is paid
[G#m]Or a talent of silver
While [A#m]I was busy here and there
The [A#]man has disappeared from [D#m]sight
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The king of Israel spoke a[A#m]loud
[D#m]That is your sentence, he de[A#m]clared
[G#m]You have pronounced it yourself [D#m]now
[G#m]The verdict rests upon your [D#m]head
[B]The prophet pulled the bandage [F#]off
[A#]And Ahab saw the prophet [D#m]face
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Your servant went into the [A#m]battle
[D#m]A prisoner was brought to [A#m]you
[B]Guard this man, they said [F#]to you
If he escapes, your life [G#m]is paid
Or a talent of sil[A#]ver
While I was busy here and there
The man has disap[D#m]peared from [B]sight
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
This is what the Lord de[F#]clares
You [C#]set the devoted man [D#m]free
Your [B]life shall stand for his [F#]life
[A#]Your people for his people
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[D#m]Sullen and angry in his [A#m]heart
[B]The king went home to [F#]Samaria
{end_of_verse}

